    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn></math> moles of a weak acid <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HA</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math> is dissolved in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">L</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>HCl</mi></math> solution. The degree of dissociation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HA</mi></math> is&nbsp;__________&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></msup></math> (Round off to the Nearest Integer). [Neglect volume change on adding <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>HA</mi></math>&nbsp;and assume degree of dissociation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#60;</mo><mo>&#60;</mo><mn>1</mn></math>]</p>",
